  "method": "Fresh pages in a separate headless Chromium browser, real full navigation per pose, deviceScaleFactor 1. A context-local diagnostic module wrapper exposed the layer. Each view waited for no pending or staged geometry, all native tiles loaded, and six unchanged diagnostic snapshots at 750ms intervals. A further 2200ms pause interval was counted before the actual screenshot. Production files were not edited by this review.",
  "observations": [
    {
      "scene": "user desktop/mobile",
      "finding": "Foreground roofs, facades, road surfaces and source paths stay visible. Daytime cream window cards no longer dominate the facade; the small reveals read dark and recessed. Broad grass areas and car silhouettes remain stylized."
    },
    {
      "scene": "courtyard desktop/mobile",
      "finding": "Quiet glazing reduces the glaring pale-on-blue checkerboard, with darker interiors and retained frame geometry. The actual inner court remains open and its ground is preserved. The camera is dominated by a very large plain gray roof with sparse repeated box equipment; this remains a content/art limitation."
    },
    {
      "scene": "waterfront desktop/mobile",
      "finding": "The source shoreline stays continuous, water has soft multidirectional ripples without the original periodic strips, and the land/road boundaries remain intact. These cameras do not frame the complete bridge, so they do not independently accept bridge continuity."
    },
    {
      "scene": "KAL desktop/mobile",
      "finding": "Bright alternating window cards are visibly subdued. The canonical facade palette is active but adjacent long panel blocks still look similar in shape, tone and window rhythm. No missing native/detailed building representation is visible in these settled frames."
    },
    {
      "scene": "MET desktop/mobile",
      "finding": "The previous repeated diagonal roof stamp remains absent. Roofs are quiet, source woodland has organic crown shapes and irregular placements, and the unknown land strip remains unchanged. Garage roofs still read as simple slabs."
    }
  ],
